    <string name="title_about">About</string>
    <string name="about_version">Version %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_what_is_title">What is PlayRetro?</string>
    <string name="about_what_is_text">PlayRetro is a classic console emulator for phones, tablets and Android TV. It organizes your game collection with box art and lets you play with a gamepad or touch controls, saving your progress automatically.\n\nIt started as an independent version of Lemuroid, the open source emulator by Filippo Scognamiglio, and runs the libretro emulation cores, the same ones used by RetroArch.</string>
    <string name="about_help_title">Help</string>
    <string name="about_license_title">License and credits</string>
    <string name="about_license_text">• PlayRetro is free software under the GNU GPL v3 license.\n• Based on Lemuroid and LibretroDroid by Filippo Scognamiglio (Swordfish90).\n• Emulation cores from libretro, each one with its own open source license.\n• System icons: \"FlatUI\" theme from RetroArch, CC BY 4.0 license.\n• Box art: libretro-thumbnails.</string>
    <string name="help_covers_question">Why is a cover missing or the name wrong?</string>
    <string name="help_covers_answer">Games are recognized by their content first. If that fails, the file name is used: name your files like \"GameName (USA).nes\", or just \"GameName.nes\". After renaming, rescan your games.</string>
